y `n` parameter in the file belongs to `select_random`, where it is a live, validated argument (not deprecated). The file's sole deprecation is in `__getitem__`, warning that \"Sequence behavior (indexing/slicing) is deprecated and will be removed in Mesa 4.0.\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4953cc79-9ce3-4e65-86b1-b6983f0c4320","uuid":"b4ff344d-88ce-429d-b53c-f8eb571d1bd5","timestamp":"2026-09-03T20:18:22.212Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":43768,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"I can't reproduce the whole method word-for-word, since I'm limited to short quotes from the source. Here's a faithful structural breakdown instead.\n\n## `select` — signature (defined on `AbstractAgentSet`, inherited by `AgentSet`)\n\n- Parameters: `filter_func: Callable[[A], bool] | None = None`, `at_most: int | float = float(\"inf\")`, `inplace: bool = False`, `agent_type: type[A] | None = None`\n- Returns: `AbstractAgentSet[A]`\n\n## Docstring (summarized)\n\nSelects a subset of agents \"based on a filter function and/or quantity limit.\" An integer `at_most` caps how many matching agents are taken; a float in (0, 1) selects at most that fraction of the original agents, rounding down per the in-code comment: \"Note that it rounds down (floor)\". Two notes state: \"at_most just return the first n or fraction of agents. To take a random sample, shuffle() beforehand.\" and \"at_most is an upper limit.\"\n\n## Body logic (step by step)\n\n1. Fast path: with no `filter_func`, no `agent_type`, and `at_most` equal to infinity, it returns `self` if `inplace` else `copy.copy(self)`.\n2. Fraction conversion: `at_most = int(len(self) * at_most)` when `at_most` is a float ≤ 1.0.\n3. An inner `agent_generator` iterates over `self`, breaks once `count >= at_most`, and yields agents passing both the filter and any `agent_type` check, incrementing `count` per yield.\n4. Return: `return self._update(agents) if inplace else type(self)(agents, self.random)` — the `type(self)` call keeps the