{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788466861-1CGEmsyp2brCVseRoxiR","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The `set` method looks fine — `setattr(agent, attr_name, value)`. So why did `agent.i` fail? \n\nOh! I see — my test: `agentset.select(at_most=0.5).set(\"i\", 42)` then `agentset.select(lambda agent: agent.i == 42)`. \n\nWait — the earlier `select(lambda agent: agent.i == 42)` iterates ALL 10 agents, and 5 of them don't have `i` at all (since only the first 5 got it set). `getattr` raises AttributeError for the others — that's the bug in MY TEST, not the library. The `select` filter `agent.i == 42` fails for agents without the attribute.\n\nRight — I should use `getattr(agent, \"i\", None) == 42`, or better, check with `agentset.get(\"i\")` or count via `sum(1 for a in agentset if getattr(a, 'i', None) == 42)`. Simplest: use a lambda with getattr default.\n\nActually, cleaner: check that exactly the first 5 agents (in order) have i == 42:\n```python\n    agentset.select(at_most=0.5).set(\"i\", 42)\n    assert [getattr(agent, \"i\", None) for agent in agentset] == [42] * 5 + [None] * 5\n```\nThat verifies both the count and that selection preserves order (first 5 selected).","signature":""}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"Together","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4953cc79-9ce3-4e65-86b1-b6983f0c4320","uuid":"4ba9cb6a-b080-47a7-9b0c-b97e4849d670","timestamp":"2026-09-03T20:21:05.979Z","request_id":"gen-1788466861-1CGEmsyp2brCVseRoxiR"}
